00:31:01,040 --> 00:31:03,950
当你去上速感培训，那个男人说，
When you go on a speed awareness
course and the man goes,

588
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,110
“要停下来要240英尺。”
"It'll take you 240 feet to stop."

589
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:08,230
你只要举手说，‘不，不是这么久。’
Just put your hand up and
go, "No, it doesn't."

590
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:11,190
我们在英国高速上得时速70英里，
We have to do 70mph in
Britain on the motorway,

591
00:31:11,240 --> 00:31:14,070
因为可能有人开福特Anglia，那车要
because somebody might have a Ford
Anglia and it will take them

592
00:31:14,120 --> 00:31:17,670
这么久才能停。但要是你开的是这好车——嘛，
that long to stop. But if you're
driving a good car like this - well,

593
00:31:17,720 --> 00:31:19,550
其实我们任何一辆——
any one of ours, really -

594
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:24,510
~ 你应该被允许跑到140...210英里每小时。~ 嗯。
~ you should be allowed to go 140... 210mph.
~ Yeah.

595
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:27,600
我不该因为有人还在开Anglia而受苦。
I shouldn't have to suffer because
somebody's still got an Anglia.

596
00:31:29,840 --> 00:31:32,950
既然已经证明我们的车能在指尖停住，
Having established that our
cars could stop on a stamp,

597
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:35,140
那我们就让它们脱缰狂奔。
we let them off the leash.

598
00:31:42,840 --> 00:31:48,040
双涡轮V6输出542马力。
542 horsepower from a twin-turbo V6.

599
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:51,720
这车简直炸裂。
It is absolutely ballistic.

600
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:59,950
当你在弯道中段，这车的中段推力是……
The mid-range thrust of this, when
you're midway through a corner,

601
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:03,070
它就是……噗——
it just... phwoar...

602
00:32:03,120 --> 00:32:05,080
它自己就发射了。
launches itself.

603
00:32:06,840 --> 00:32:09,670
我觉得在这儿，你可以让一些相当不错的跑车大吃一惊
I think in this you could give
some pretty good sports cars

604
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:11,720
一次相当大的惊喜。
a pretty big surprise.

605
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:20,430
早期的宝马M车型听起来就像
In the early days, BMW's
M cars sounded like

606
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,790
五百码的撕裂帆布声
500 yards of ripping calico

607
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:27,230
而且方向盘像有心灵感应一样，真是太棒了。
and they had telepathic steering
and they were magnificent.

608
00:32:27,280 --> 00:32:29,470
不过，近年来，
In recent years, though,

609
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:31,710
有些魔力好像已经消失了。
some of the magic has sort of gone.

610
00:32:31,760 --> 00:32:34,600
不过这款车，魔力又回来了。
With this one, though, it is back.

611
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:39,840
真的回来了。
It is properly back.

612
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:48,360
天啊，这简直……电力十足，好得不要不要的。
God, this is just...
electrifyingly good.

613
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:52,870
很快，制作组叫我们靠边停下，准备参加某种赛车活动。
Soon the producers
told us to pull over

614
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:56,310
我好奇这到底是什么样的活动呢？
for some kind of motor racing event.

615
00:32:56,360 --> 00:32:59,300
当我们抵达时，谜团更深了。
What manner of thing
will it be, I wonder?

616
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:02,670
而且还被发了套蠢萌的安全防护服。
The mystery deepened when we arrived

617
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:06,320
不过随后真相大白。
and were given idiotic
health and safety outfits.

618
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:10,240
天呐！
But then all was revealed.

619
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:16,600
用于建造现代中国的大部分钢材
Holy cow!

620
00:33:21,520 --> 00:33:24,230
都来自这片巨大的坑洞。
Most of the steel used
to build modern China

621
00:33:24,280 --> 00:33:27,950
但今天，它将成为我们的赛道。
came out of this vast
hole in the ground.

622
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:31,800
一定是上坡赛。
But today it would be our racetrack.

623
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:36,550
~ 像古德伍德。
~ 对，正是。
~ 并不是完全像……
~ 不完全是的。
Must be a hill climb.

624
00:33:36,600 --> 00:33:39,990
每一个弯角都有个…致命的跌落。哦，你好。
~ Like Goodwood.
~ Yeah, it is.
~ It's not exactly like...
~ Not exactly, no.

625
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:45,350
哦，是你啊。
Every single corner has got a drop
on it that's... lethal. Oh, hello.

626
00:33:45,400 --> 00:33:47,000
“现在请轮流驾驭上坡赛道……”
Oh, it's you.

627
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:51,070
~ 是的，没错。
~ ……试图打破标杆时间。
"You will now take it in turns to
drive up the hill climb course..."

628
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:54,910
~ 我猜，标杆时间是斯提格定的？
~ 不是斯提格。
~ It is, yeah.
~ ".. attempting to beat a benchmark time."

629
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:58,910
但其实是……斯提格的澳洲表亲。
~ Let me guess, the benchmark
time is set by The Stig?
~ It isn't The Stig.

630
00:33:58,960 --> 00:34:02,670
~ 他比英国的斯提格还大。
~ 嗯。
But it is... The Stig's
Australian cousin.

631
00:34:08,640 --> 00:34:11,110
而且他的……香肠更大。
~ He's bigger than English Stig.
~ Mm.

632
00:34:11,160 --> 00:34:13,870
~ 你怎么知道的？
~ 看吧。
And he's got a bigger... sausage.

633
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,910
~ 从这里就能看出他是个……
~ 大斯提格。
~ How did you find that out?
~ Well, look.

634
00:34:15,960 --> 00:34:20,080
大斯提格将会抛出挑战
~ Even from here, one can see that he is a...
~ Big Stig.

635
00:34:21,200 --> 00:34:23,590
在一辆典型的澳洲跑车上——
Big Stig would be laying
down the gauntlet

636
00:34:23,640 --> 00:34:26,190
一辆霍顿皮卡。
in a typical Aussie sportscar -

637
00:34:26,240 --> 00:34:28,480
~ 你知道它叫啥的，那辆马卢？
~ 知道。
a Holden Ute.

638
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:32,790
~ 它的马力比我的宝马还高。
~ 真有吗？
~ 多了两匹马力。
~ You know that, whatever it's called, Maloo?
~ Yeah.

639
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:37,040
三、二、一，发！
~ It's got more horsepower than my BMW.
~ Has it?
~ Two more.

640
00:34:38,600 --> 00:34:41,030
Three, two, one, go!
Three, two, one, go!

641
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:50,640
哇塞，这画面真是光彩夺目！
Whoa, that's a spectacular
thing to look at.

642
00:34:56,800 --> 00:35:00,720
~ 哎呀不！
~ 哎呀，他那边有点偏了。怎么……？
~ Oh, no!
~ Oh, he's gone a bit sideways there. What...?

643
00:35:06,320 --> 00:35:09,720
~ 我是唯一一个真的喜欢那辆Ute的人吗？
~ 是的，你是。
~ 行。
~ Am I the only one who really likes that Ute?
~ Yes, you are.
~ OK.

644
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:15,910
他们准备好，稳住，接着……
And they're ready, steady, and...

645
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,390
冲过终点线。
across the line.

646
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:20,640
天呐，真是......呃，够呛。
Gordon Bennett, he was... Oof.

647
00:35:21,800 --> 00:35:24,670
等大斯提格的尘土落定后，我们三个人
As Big Stig's dust settled,
the three of us

648
00:35:24,720 --> 00:35:27,520
一路走到矿井底部。
made our way to the
bottom of the mine.

649
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:31,030
~ 我一定会赢。
~ 我真怀疑。
~ I'll win this.
~ I seriously doubt that.

650
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:33,790
~ 好啊，我会的或者他会的，因为我们有四驱。
~ 说得对。
~ Well, I will or he will cos
we've got four-wheel drive.
~ It's true.

651
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:36,630
四驱在拖拉机上有用，但在普通道路车上
Four-wheel drive is useful on a
tractor but on a normal road car

652
00:35:36,680 --> 00:35:39,750
~ 没意义，跟水一样。
~ 跟水怎么一样？
~ it's pointless. It's like water.
~ How's it like water?

653
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:42,630
因为它既不利也不弊，根本没起作用。
Cos it's neither good nor bad,
it just doesn't do anything.

654
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:44,950
水倒是能派上不少用场。
Water's useful for a lot of things.

655
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:48,190
只要往里加点啤酒花或者葡萄倒是行。但单独的……
It is if you put hops in it,
or grapes. But on its own...

656
00:35:48,240 --> 00:35:50,510
最近一次后驱车
When was the last time
a rear-wheel drive car

657
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:52,590
赢得世界拉力锦标赛是什么时候？
won the World Rally Championship?

658
00:35:52,640 --> 00:35:55,070
~ 哈？
~ 哦……最近吧。
~ Huh!
~ Oh... recently.

659
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:57,430
~ 没那么近。
~ 在我脑子里是的。
~ Not that recently.
~ In my mind, it was.

660
00:35:57,480 --> 00:35:59,630
~ 是1983年，那简直是昨天。
~ 对。
~ It was 1983 and that was yesterday.
~ Correct.

661
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:02,110
从那以后就全是四驱了。
Ever since then it's been four-wheel.

662
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:04,990
~ 那是拉力赛段吧？
~ 我先来一段。
~ That's a rally stage, isn't it?
~ I shall do this first.

663
00:36:05,040 --> 00:36:07,840
~ 你将见证诗一般的驾驭。
~ 开始吧。
~ And you will witness poetry.
~ Fire away.

664
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:14,030
在一群茫然的矿工面前，我准备开始我的冲刺。
In front of a crowd of bemused
miners, I prepared for my run.

665
00:36:14,080 --> 00:36:16,590
牵引控制……关掉。
Traction control... off.

666
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:19,200
三、二、一，冲！
Three, two, one, go!

667
00:36:21,640 --> 00:36:24,310
已经在找抓地力了！
It's struggling for traction already!

668
00:36:24,960 --> 00:36:28,550
第二段，还在打转轮子。第三段！
Second, still spinning
the wheels. Third!

669
00:36:28,600 --> 00:36:30,750
还在打转轮子。
Still spinning the wheels.

670
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:34,390
也许我该把牵引控制开着。
Maybe I should have kept
the traction control on.

671
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:37,270
哦——！
Ohhh!

672
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:38,670
滑溜溜的。
Slithering.

673
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:40,190
大滑！
Big slide.

674
00:36:42,600 --> 00:36:44,070
天呐！
God above.

675
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,990
要是，突然——嘭——
What if, all of a sudden - twoo! -

676
00:36:47,040 --> 00:36:49,310
然后我们直接看到宝马的底盘。
and then we just saw the
underside of the BMW.

677
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:51,700
可以检查一下排气管还行不行。
Could check the exhaust is OK.

678
00:36:57,800 --> 00:37:02,440
来吧，宝马，给我那575马力！
Come on, Beemer, give
me that 575 horsepower!

679
00:37:05,760 --> 00:37:08,230
四驱是给弱者用的。
Four-wheel drive is for the weak.

680
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:11,320
180公里/小时！
180kph!

681
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:16,400
穿过卡车，冲过终点线！
And through the lorries
and across the line!

682
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:20,750
下一个，宾利。
Next, the Bentley.

683
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:23,950
还有马尔堡公爵那座宏伟的乡间宅邸
And the magnificent country residence
of the Duke of Marlborough

684
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,350
也来到起点位置。
takes its place on the starting line.

685
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:30,150
我把悬挂调得稍微软一点。
I'm going to bias the suspension
slightly towards soft.

686
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:32,230
这样可能会抓地更好。
I might get more traction that way.

687
00:37:32,280 --> 00:37:35,830
三、二、一，起！
Three, two, one, go!

688
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:39,440
抓地，抓地，抓地！好车。
Grip, grip, grip! Good girl.

689
00:37:42,280 --> 00:37:45,150
仅仅100米后，
After just 100 metres,

690
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:49,440
四驱宾利已经领先宝马四秒。
the four-wheel drive Bentley was
four seconds ahead of the BMW.

691
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:52,540
进弯。
Into the hairpin.

692
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:58,760
哦，四驱在那儿帮了大忙，简直太好玩了。
Oh, four-wheel drive helping
me round that a treat.

693
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:04,700
弯道。
Hairpin.

694
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:10,350
瓷器和银器要掉下来
The China and silverware
is going to fall over

695
00:38:10,400 --> 00:38:14,300
让管家以后收拾一团烂摊子。
and make a terrible mess for
the butler to clear up later.

696
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:19,160
好了，刹车，准备……天啊，转弯……
Right, braking, ready for
the... Oh, God, turn here...

697
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:22,990
来啊，咬住！好了。
Come on, bite! There you go.

698
00:38:31,360 --> 00:38:32,790
好了，观众们，现在我们单挑，
Right, viewers, now we're alone,

699
00:38:32,840 --> 00:38:35,030
看，那车本该是这条赛道最快的
look, that car should be
the fastest up that course

700
00:38:35,080 --> 00:38:37,950
但凭全世界最强的意志，我可不打算，
but with the best will in the
world, I'm not going to be,

701
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:39,870
所以我已经有计策了。
so I've got a plan.

702
00:38:42,280 --> 00:38:46,030
英版斯提格，我已经带他转了好几天。
English Stig. I've been carrying
him around for days.

703
00:38:46,080 --> 00:38:48,590
把英版斯提格偷偷塞进驾驶位，
With English Stig smuggled
into the driving seat,

704
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:51,990
GT‑R已准备好出发。
the GT-R readied for the off.

705
00:38:52,040 --> 00:38:53,910
看吧，他在这儿。"你好。"
Here he is, look. "Hello."

706
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:57,760
三、二、一，起！
Three, two, one, go!

707
00:39:03,200 --> 00:39:05,870
~ 这起步真够激烈的。
~ 你好！
~ That's quite a vigorous start.
~ Hello!

708
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:16,180
~ 嗯……那是赛车轨迹，你看到没？
~ 看见了。
~ Um...that was a racing
line, there, did you see?
~ Yeah.

709
00:39:22,720 --> 00:39:26,000
~ 我看到的根本不…
~ 合情合理吗？
~ …是可能的。
~ None of what I'm seeing...
~ Makes sense?
~ .. is possible.

710
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:39,280
~ 天哪。
~ 他在抽搐，竟然……
~ 我的天……！
~ Oh, my God.
~ He's twitching, he's actually...
~ Oh, my...!

711
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:46,670
他要去哪儿？
Where's he going?

712
00:39:46,720 --> 00:39:51,020
他忘了终点在哪儿……好吧，他干了点詹姆斯·梅式的事。
He forgot where the end... Well,
he did something James May-ish.

713
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:57,390
非常感谢。
Thanks very much.

714
00:39:57,440 --> 00:39:59,000
他来了。
Here he is.

715
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:05,390
~ 那速度真快。
~ 嗯。
~ 挺有力的。
~ 四驱。
~ That was very quick.
~ Yeah.
~ It was vigorous.
~ Four-wheel drive.

716
00:40:05,440 --> 00:40:08,030
~ 这车不错，挺讨喜的。
~ 确实。
~ 我不是在说…
~ It's a good car. It flatters.
~ It does.
~ I'm not saying...

717
00:40:08,080 --> 00:40:11,350
~ 你这么说也对。我……你知道，我本来没那么自信，
You're right to say it. I... You
know, I wasn't that confident,

718
00:40:11,400 --> 00:40:14,550
~ 但它真的一路照顾着你。
~ 我们这儿已经有成绩了。
~ but it does look after you all the way.
~ We have the times here anyway.

719
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:18,600
澳洲斯提格驾驶HSV Maloo跑出1分17秒8。
The Australian Stig in the
HSV Maloo did a 1:17.8.

720
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:24,350
~ 看来我稍慢了一点。
~ 真的吗？
~ 说说看。
~ I was a little bit slower,
as it's turned out.
~ Really?
~ Go on.

721
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:25,510
他是1分17秒8。
He was 1:17.8.

722
00:40:25,560 --> 00:40:27,270
我则是1分31秒6。
I was 1:31.6.

723
00:40:27,320 --> 00:40:29,430
这不是慢了点吗？
That is slower, isn't it?

724
00:40:29,480 --> 00:40:32,990
宾利……1分18秒6。
Bentley... 1:18.6.

725
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:35,870
~ 哦，还不错。
~ 挺好的。
~ Oh, that's not bad.
~ That's pretty good.

726
00:40:35,920 --> 00:40:37,150
我对这个挺满意的。
I'm pleased with that.

727
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:39,430
你真的……只差一秒。
You were really... You
were only a second off.

728
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:40,710
我在那辆老宾利上也是这么来的。
I was on it on the old Bentley.

729
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:44,000
GT-R。1分13秒3。
GT-R. 1:13.3.

730
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:48,960
比斯提格快了四秒半。
Four and a half seconds
faster than a Stig.

731
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:52,320
~ 干得好啊。
~ 谢了。
~ Well done, you.
~ Thank you.

732
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:57,390
‘当我们重新上路时，我还能接受……
'As we got back on the
road, I could accept that

733
00:40:57,440 --> 00:41:00,950
‘四驱在铁矿里倒是合情合理。
'four-wheel drive makes
sense in an iron ore mine.

734
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,310
‘不过詹姆斯的成绩……
'But James's time...

735
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:04,320
‘不行。
'no.

736
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:08,880
1分13秒，詹姆斯·梅。
1 minute 13 seconds, James May.

737
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:14,790
詹姆斯·梅一般要花1分13秒才能穿过一道门。
It normally takes James May 1 minute
13 seconds to go through a door.

738
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:16,150
他是怎么做到的？
How did he do that?

739
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:20,240
‘更关键的是，我们的车是怎么做到的？'
'And more to the point,
how did our cars do that?'

740
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:24,110
要让这辆宾利在那坡道上硬冲，
To be in this Bentley
hammering up that hill,

741
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:27,670
这可是对现代豪华车的极大考验，
you're asking a lot
of a modern luxury car

742
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:29,710
它的重量足足有两吨半左右。
weighing the best part
of two and a half tonnes.

743
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:31,230
它居然干成了。
It did it.

744
00:41:33,520 --> 00:41:35,750
‘经历了一天的尘土与污秽，
'After a dirty, dusty day,

745
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:39,680
‘我们本来期待能住进一家真的酒店。
'we were looking forward to
staying in an actual hotel.

746
00:41:41,280 --> 00:41:45,270
‘可惜，这里是几英里内唯一的一家。
'Sadly, though, this was
the only one for miles.'

747
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:49,320
~ 晚上好。
~ 晚上好。
~ Evening.
~ Evening.

748
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:55,270
~ 那是床吗？
~ 是吗？
~ 对。
~ Is that a bed?
~ Is it?
~ Yeah.

749
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:59,840
‘于是杰里米建议我们立刻离开……
'Jeremy, therefore, suggested
we should leave immediately...

750
00:42:03,360 --> 00:42:07,240
‘……尝试一种他刚灵机一动的新式露营方式。
'.. and try a new type of tenting
that he'd just thought of.'

751
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:12,710
你在干嘛？
What are you doing?

752
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:16,470
~ 大多数人会先生火，然后围着坐，对吧？
~ 对。
~ Most people build a campfire
and then sit around it, yes?
~ Yes.

753
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:20,510
我干的事是把篝火砸在我们周围。
What I've done is built
the campfire round us.

754
00:42:20,560 --> 00:42:21,950
于是我们可以坐在中间，
So we can sit in the middle,

755
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:23,590
烤我们的沙门氏菌
cook our salmonella

756
00:42:23,640 --> 00:42:26,990
这样所有凶猛动物都进不来。
and none of all the dangerous
animals can get at us.

757
00:42:27,040 --> 00:42:30,310
我已经把露营方式彻底革命了。
I have revolutionised tenting,
is what I've done.

758
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:31,750
等下。
Hang on.

759
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:35,270
~ 你现在在干嘛？
~ 点火最好的办法是什么？
~ What are you doing now?
~ What's the best way of starting a fire?

760
00:42:35,320 --> 00:42:37,350
汽油。
Petrol.

761
00:42:37,400 --> 00:42:40,520
从那颗脑袋里看世界会是什么样的？
What must the world look
like from inside that head?

762
00:42:42,840 --> 00:42:44,710
~ 准备好了吗？
~ 准备好了。
~ Are you ready?
~ Yes.

763
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:52,590
看啊！我把火弄得四周都是！
Behold! For I have made
fire all around us!

764
00:42:52,640 --> 00:42:54,590
~ 太棒了，杰里米…
~ 真是热得不行。
~ 什么？
~ Brilliant. Jeremy...
~ It's quite warm.
~ What?

765
00:42:54,640 --> 00:42:55,870
传统篝火的众多好处之一是
One of the many advantages of

766
00:42:55,920 --> 00:42:58,110
围坐在唯一的传统篝火旁时，
a single traditional campfire
that you sit round

767
00:42:58,160 --> 00:43:00,670
你可以躲开烟雾的方向。
is that you can move out of the
way of where the smoke is going.

768
00:43:00,720 --> 00:43:03,750
是啊。我的篝火不行，但我们安全。蹲低点。
Yeah. You can't with mine,
but we are safe. Get down low.

769
00:43:03,800 --> 00:43:05,750
~ 蹲低点。更好。
~ 我已经蹲低了。
~ Down low. It's better.
~ I already am down low.

770
00:43:05,800 --> 00:43:07,630
~ 更糟糕。
~ 不，这里更好。
~ It's worse.
~ No, it's better here.

771
00:43:07,680 --> 00:43:10,830
~ 不管怎样…
~ 什么？
~ 帐篷在哪儿？
~ Anyway...
~ What?
~ Where are the tents?

772
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:12,910
就在车里。
In the cars.

773
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:14,960
~ 好吧…
~ 你这死笨蛋。
~ Well...
~ You plum sack.

774
00:43:19,360 --> 00:43:22,190
“第二天早上，经历了又一个糟糕的夜晚后，
'The next morning, after
another dreadful night,

775
00:43:22,240 --> 00:43:24,800
我们又上路了。
'we were back on the road.

776
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:28,350
“大约四个小时后，
'And after about four hours,

777
00:43:28,400 --> 00:43:31,990
哈蒙德教授终于意识到了些什么。”
'Professor Hammond finally
realised something.'

778
00:43:33,480 --> 00:43:35,880
太大了。澳大利亚，真是大。
It's big. It is big, Australia.

779
00:43:37,480 --> 00:43:41,550
“我们要去那座巨大的养牛场，
'We were headed for the gigantic
farm where we'd be herding cattle,

780
00:43:41,600 --> 00:43:45,590
决定要在一天内赶到。”
'and had decided to try
and reach it in one day.

781
00:43:45,640 --> 00:43:49,200
“这段路程…将会是巨大的。”
'The drive would be... enormous.'

782
00:43:50,320 --> 00:43:53,870
我用小眼睛发现了点以 T 开头的东西。
I spy with my little eye
something beginning with T.

783
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:55,120
树。
Tree.

784
00:43:56,440 --> 00:43:59,230
我用小眼睛发现了点以 T 开头的东西。
I spy with my little eye
something beginning with T.

785
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:01,000
白蚁丘。
Termite mound.

786
00:44:02,920 --> 00:44:05,310
我用小眼睛发现了点以 T 开头的东西。
I spy with my little eye
something beginning with T.

787
00:44:05,360 --> 00:44:07,500
是“树”。别闹了！
It's "tree". Just stop it!

788
00:44:08,360 --> 00:44:10,150
“哈蒙德不想配合，
'Since Hammond wouldn't play,

789
00:44:10,200 --> 00:44:14,430
我只能调到收得到的唯一电台。”
'I tuned into the only station
that my radio could receive.'

790
00:44:14,480 --> 00:44:18,350
“从达尔文运往印尼的轻体小母牛
'.. lightweight heifers out
of Darwin heading to Indonesia

791
00:44:18,400 --> 00:44:21,950
现在的售价高达每公斤2.25美元。
'are now fetching up to 2.25 a kilo.

792
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:27,070
肥育阉牛运往印尼，最高每公斤2.45美元。”
'Fattening steers heading to
Indonesia up to 2.45 a kilo.'

793
00:44:27,120 --> 00:44:30,160
你怎么不放点 Steely Dan ？
Why don't you play Steely Dan?!

794
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:34,830
“在澳洲这块儿，通常还能碰到点刺激的事
'Normally you get SOME excitement
in this part of Australia

795
00:44:34,880 --> 00:44:39,520
比如要超车一大串巨型载货列车。”
'when you have to overtake a
convoy of gigantic road trains.'

796
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:49,840
“其实我们挺期待这场惊险的。”
'We were actually quite looking
forward to the peril.'

797
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:58,510
这儿尘土飞扬。
A lot of dust coming up here.

798
00:44:58,560 --> 00:45:02,350
“不过在我们这辆快车上，简直小菜一碟。”
'But in cars as fast as
ours, it was a doddle.'

799
00:45:02,400 --> 00:45:04,670
我躲开了，轻松多了。
I'm out of the way. I'm free.

800
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:10,830
“一点钟，我吃了一顿美味的澳洲午餐。”
'At one o'clock, I had
a delicious Aussie lunch.'

801
00:45:10,880 --> 00:45:12,990
这玩意儿热得要命。
"Bloody hot ring-burner."

802
00:45:13,040 --> 00:45:16,040
然后又回到老本行，照常进行。
'And then it was back
to business as usual.'

803
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:20,430
C2 那批小母牛的卖价在160到176之间。
'C2 heifers sell from 160-176.

804
00:45:20,480 --> 00:45:22,990
轻量级的C3小母牛飙升了四块。
'Lightweight C3 heifers lifted four.

805
00:45:23,040 --> 00:45:25,150
它们的售价在160到190之间。
'They sell from 160-190.

806
00:45:25,200 --> 00:45:29,150
而重型小母牛甚至冲到204美分……
'And heavyweight heifers
returned up to 204 cents...'

807
00:45:29,200 --> 00:45:31,280
哎呀，天啊！
Oh, God!

808
00:45:43,960 --> 00:45:45,230
天色已暗
'Darkness had fallen

809
00:45:45,280 --> 00:45:49,870
我们终于到达农场车道的尽头时。
'when we finally reached the
bottom of the farm drive.'

810
00:45:49,920 --> 00:45:51,460
这可真是乐不可支！
Joy of joys!

811
00:45:53,920 --> 00:45:57,510
但是……又花了两个小时才到达
'But...it took another
two hours to reach

812
00:45:57,560 --> 00:46:00,550
那座位于山顶的农舍……
'the farmhouse at the top of it...'

813
00:46:00,600 --> 00:46:01,990
~ 欢迎。  
~ 谢谢。
~ Welcome.
~ Thank you.

814
00:46:02,040 --> 00:46:04,430
…那里根本没有空余的卧室。
'.. where there were
no spare bedrooms.

815
00:46:04,480 --> 00:46:09,160
于是我决定再搞点新花样露营。
'So I decided to try another
new sort of tenting.'

816
00:46:10,680 --> 00:46:15,550
~ 你知道吗？  
~ 什么？  
~ 我们开始了这个，我三台车都喜欢。
~ Do you know what?
~ What?
~ We started this, I liked all three cars.

817
00:46:15,600 --> 00:46:17,470
我至今仍然喜欢。
I still do.

818
00:46:17,520 --> 00:46:21,190
但我对宾利是最好的信念现在已经铁板钉钉了。
But my conviction that the Bentley
is the best is now absolute.

819
00:46:21,240 --> 00:46:22,390
就只是……
I just...

820
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:25,510
~ 我仍然觉得它有点……  
~ 什么？
~ I still find it slightly sort of...
~ What?

821
00:46:25,560 --> 00:46:28,350
它带着一点假装贵族的味儿，
There's a slight hint of
faux-toffery about it,

822
00:46:28,400 --> 00:46:30,230
这显然跟你这身板子太配了。
which suits you very well, obviously.

823
00:46:30,280 --> 00:46:32,190
不过尼桑的好处是
But the great thing
about the Nissan is

824
00:46:32,240 --> 00:46:34,990
它就是一把精心调校的驾驶工具。
it's just a finely honed
driving instrument.

825
00:46:35,040 --> 00:46:37,830
好吧，不是……好吧，在纽博格林，你的那台……
Well, no... OK, on the
Nurburgring, yours is...

826
00:46:37,880 --> 00:46:39,310
别提纽博格林了。
Don't mention the Nurburgring.

827
00:46:39,360 --> 00:46:41,990
~ 这不就是为此准备的，詹姆斯。  
~ 不是的，才不是。  
~ 杰里米，你的BMW。
~ That's what it's for, James.
~ No, it's not.
~ And Jeremy, your BM.

828
00:46:42,040 --> 00:46:44,070
~ 看起来的确很棒。  
~ 好了，给你。
~ It does look brilliant.
~ There you go.

829
00:46:44,120 --> 00:46:46,110
这辆BMW相当称职。
It's a very competent
motorcar, the BMW.

830
00:46:46,160 --> 00:46:48,470
这叫淡淡的贬低，却是称赞，梅说的。
That's damning with faint
praise, that is, May.

831
00:46:48,520 --> 00:46:49,790
对，没错。
Yes, exactly.

832
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:52,230
你的有点儿过于 Dolce & Gabbana（时髦）了。
Yours is a bit too Dolce & Gabbana.

833
00:46:52,280 --> 00:46:54,030
你的有点儿像 Poundland（廉价）了。
Yours is a bit too Poundland.

834
00:46:54,080 --> 00:46:57,110
它们都是绝佳的车，别说错了。
They're both brilliant
cars, make no mistake.

835
00:46:57,160 --> 00:47:00,230
~ 顺便问一下，你在干嘛？  
~ Claymore。那是地雷。
~ What are you doing, by the way?
~ Claymores. They're mines.

836
00:47:00,280 --> 00:47:01,550
我把它们从英国带来的。
I brought them from Britain.

837
00:47:01,600 --> 00:47:04,310
在我们营地周围埋上Claymore。
Ring our campsite with claymores.

838
00:47:04,360 --> 00:47:06,790
然后任何走来的动物……
Then any animal that comes...

839
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:09,640
…它们会……变成薄壳。
.. they will... it
will become a veneer.

840
00:47:11,640 --> 00:47:15,550
'等我干完活，梅和哈蒙德把啤酒全喝光了，'
'When my work was done and May and
Hammond had drunk all the beer,

841
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:17,870
我们今晚收营了。
'we turned in for the night.'

842
00:47:23,200 --> 00:47:26,480
~ 什么声音？！
~ 那是我救你命的声音。
~ What was that?!
~ That was the sound of me saving your life.

843
00:47:30,800 --> 00:47:35,520
第二天早上，我们的营地看起来像屠宰场。
'The next morning, our campsite
looks like an abattoir.'

844
00:47:37,920 --> 00:47:41,270
~ 这是什么？
~ 鳄鱼的耳朵。
~ What's this?
~ Crocodile's ear.

845
00:47:41,320 --> 00:47:44,310
~ 它长毛的。
~ 鳄鱼的确有毛耳朵。
~ It's hairy.
~ Crocodiles do have hairy ears.

846
00:47:44,360 --> 00:47:45,710
它们甚至根本没有耳朵。
They don't even have ears.

847
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:48,630
有的，那是一条想把我们吃掉的鳄鱼。
They do. That was a crocodile
that was coming to eat us.

848
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:50,870
而我的克雷莫地雷救了我们的命。
And my claymore saved our lives.

849
00:47:50,920 --> 00:47:52,390
哈蒙德，你看看我们这儿捡到啥了。
Look what we've got here, Hammond.

850
00:47:52,440 --> 00:47:53,870
这是鳄鱼的蹄子！
It's a crocodile's hoof(!)

851
00:47:53,920 --> 00:47:57,070
你把那头农场的奶牛炸了。
You've detonated one
of the man's cows.

852
00:47:57,120 --> 00:48:00,790
别老是纠结“哎呀，炸了”这种事，行吧？
Let's not get bogged down
with..."ooh, blew up," all right?

853
00:48:00,840 --> 00:48:04,270
因为我一直在研究这块农场。
Because I've been reading
about this farm.

854
00:48:04,320 --> 00:48:08,710
~ 是的。
~ 其实它有320万英亩。
~ Yes.
~ It's actually 3.2 million acres.

855
00:48:08,760 --> 00:48:11,430
那又多了20万英亩，就这么悄悄冒出来的？
So another 200,000 acres
just slipped in there?

856
00:48:11,480 --> 00:48:13,190
要是把它放在对比里看，
And to put that in perspective,

857
00:48:13,240 --> 00:48:17,990
这座农场的面积跟白金汉郡…一样大。
this single farm is the same
size as Buckinghamshire...

858
00:48:18,040 --> 00:48:20,670
还有赫特福德郡…以及萨里郡…
and Hertfordshire... and Surrey...

859
00:48:20,720 --> 00:48:24,710
再加上东萨塞克斯、西萨塞克斯和肯特，合在一起。
and East Sussex and West
Sussex and Kent, combined.

860
00:48:24,760 --> 00:48:28,480
它跟英格兰东南部的面积相当！
It's the same size as the
South East of England!

861
00:48:31,800 --> 00:48:37,240
这里看到的所有东西，甚至还有更多，都是同一座农场。
'Everything you see here, and
a lot more besides, is one farm.

862
00:48:40,080 --> 00:48:42,990
当我们出发去赶牛时，
'And as we set off
to do cattle herding,

863
00:48:43,040 --> 00:48:45,550
我们仍然在苦苦挣扎
'we were still struggling
to get our heads

864
00:48:45,600 --> 00:48:48,000
面对这巨大的规模。
'around the enormity of it all.'

865
00:48:49,160 --> 00:48:53,550
从这座农场到最近的超市要有250英里。
It's 250 miles from this farm
to the nearest supermarket.

866
00:48:53,600 --> 00:48:57,190
这相当于从伦敦开车到纽卡斯尔。
That's like driving from
London to Newcastle

867
00:48:57,240 --> 00:49:01,430
只是为了买点洗碗液和厕纸。
just to buy some washing-up
liquid and some bog roll.

868
00:49:01,480 --> 00:49:03,590
而且还不是走高速公路。
And it's not driving on motorways.

869
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:06,940
既不是A1也不是M1，而是土路。
It's not the A1 and it's
not the M1, it's tracks.

870
00:49:09,120 --> 00:49:14,600
在英国，普通的牛群大概有28到50头牛。
In Britain, the average beef herd
is between, sort of, 28 and 50 cows.

871
00:49:15,880 --> 00:49:18,520
而这里却有6.4万头。
And here it's 64,000.

872
00:49:22,280 --> 00:49:25,070
我们的任务是把其中4000头赶回来，
'Our task was to round
up 4,000 of them,

873
00:49:25,120 --> 00:49:28,420
我们以为这么多牛很容易找得到。
'and we assumed this many
would be easy to spot.'

874
00:49:29,680 --> 00:49:34,470
~ 现在，你把悬挂调高了吗，哈蒙德？
~ 是的，我已经调好了。
~ Now, have you raised your
suspension up, Hammond?
~ Yes, I have.

875
00:49:34,520 --> 00:49:38,520
~ 你看到牛了吗？
~ 没有，一个也没有。
~ Can you see any cows?
~ No, no. Not one.

876
00:49:39,720 --> 00:49:42,150
但我们可能在相当于多佛的地方
But we could be in the
equivalent of Dover

877
00:49:42,200 --> 00:49:44,070
而牛却可能在比肯斯菲尔德。
and the cows could
be in Beaconsfield.

878
00:49:44,120 --> 00:49:45,950
好吧，我正想说这个。
Well, I was just thinking that.

879
00:49:46,000 --> 00:49:48,710
要是它们全部在对面角落呢？
What if they're all in
the opposite corner?

880
00:49:48,760 --> 00:49:51,960
它们可能在离这里一百英里外。
They could be 100 miles
away from here.

881
00:49:54,920 --> 00:49:58,230
'连高科技的宝马都帮不上忙。'
'Even the hi-tech BMW was no help.'

882
00:49:58,280 --> 00:50:03,030
'语音指令。新条目。拼写地点的名字。'
'Voice commands. New entry.
Spell name of place.'

883
00:50:03,080 --> 00:50:04,590
几头牛。
Some cows.

884
00:50:04,640 --> 00:50:06,590
'你是说羊丘吗？'
'Did you mean Sheep Hills?'

885
00:50:06,640 --> 00:50:09,030
不是羊，是牛。
No, not sheep. Cows.

886
00:50:09,080 --> 00:50:11,870
吸引牛的那个声音怎么叫？
What's the noise you
make to attract a cow?

887
00:50:11,920 --> 00:50:14,150
要是狗的话会是...
If it was a dog it would be...

888
00:50:14,200 --> 00:50:16,350
我对牛一窍不通...
I don't know anything about cows...

889
00:50:16,400 --> 00:50:18,800
除了它们的味道之外。
apart from what they taste like.

890
00:50:20,760 --> 00:50:25,640
找不到牛，还想当牛仔真是难啊。
It is difficult to be a cowboy
when we can't find any cows.

891
00:50:28,320 --> 00:50:30,260
外面气温41度。
41 degrees out there.

892
00:50:32,680 --> 00:50:34,020
没有牛。
No cows.

893
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:40,750
'转了一个小时以后，终于捡到金子了。'
'After an hour's meandering about,
however, we struck gold.'

894
00:50:40,800 --> 00:50:42,190
牛！
Cow!

895
00:50:42,240 --> 00:50:44,670
那边。对，牛！
Over there. Yes, cows!

896
00:50:44,720 --> 00:50:47,230
我数到四头牛。
I'm counting four cows.

897
00:50:47,280 --> 00:50:50,590
算是个开头。把它们抓起来，围成一圈。
That is a start. Get
'em, round 'em up.

898
00:50:50,640 --> 00:50:53,740
你们俩去侧翼，我在后面守着。
You two take the flanks,
I'll stay at the rear.

899
00:50:59,720 --> 00:51:03,790
别靠太近。慌了它们会跑，炸了我们的牛排。
Don't get too close. If you panic
'em, you'll spoil the burgers.

900
00:51:03,840 --> 00:51:05,710
抓住了，抓住了。
We've got them. We have them.

901
00:51:05,760 --> 00:51:07,500
完美。
This is perfect.

902
00:51:11,800 --> 00:51:13,950
我们这玩意儿真是太牛了！
We're brilliant at this!

903
00:51:14,000 --> 00:51:15,800
'但是……'
'But then...'

904
00:51:17,560 --> 00:51:19,870
它们要刹车然后跑进树林。
They're going to brake
and go in the woods.

905
00:51:19,920 --> 00:51:22,830
它们把头钻进树里！
They're getting into the trees!

906
00:51:22,880 --> 00:51:25,480
我进不去，太崎岖了。
I can't go in there. It's too rough.

907
00:51:26,120 --> 00:51:28,310
'虽然哈蒙德有四驱，'
'And even though Hammond
had four-wheel drive,

908
00:51:28,360 --> 00:51:31,590
'结果他也进不去。'
'it turned out he couldn't
go in there either.'

909
00:51:35,560 --> 00:51:37,300
呃，我卡住了。
Um, I'm beached.

910
00:51:37,960 --> 00:51:41,030
'等詹姆斯把他拉出来的时候……'
'And by the time James
had pulled him out...'

911
00:51:41,080 --> 00:51:43,920
三、二、一。开拍！
Three, two, one. Action!

912
00:51:47,800 --> 00:51:50,340
'……我们那四头牛跑丢了。'
'..our four cows had wandered off.'

913
00:51:53,120 --> 00:51:56,150
情况报告——我们找到了四头牛，却又把它们弄丢了。
Sitrep - we found four
cows and we lost them.

914
00:51:56,200 --> 00:52:02,440
'那我们找到四千头牛时还有几率？'
'So, what chance would we
have when we found 4,000?'

915
00:52:11,080 --> 00:52:12,470
对。
Right.

916
00:52:12,520 --> 00:52:14,120
对。
Right.

917
00:52:15,440 --> 00:52:19,190
现在，这是我这辈子见过的最大的一群牛
Now, this is the biggest
flock of cows

918
00:52:19,240 --> 00:52:22,000
我这辈子见过的。
I have ever seen in my entire life.

919
00:52:25,960 --> 00:52:28,870
'我们的任务是把它们全拐个向头
'Our job was to get
them all turned round

920
00:52:28,920 --> 00:52:33,400
然后把它们赶进一个距离十公里的巨型围栏……'
'and then herd them into a giant
pen, which was 10km away...

921
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:38,920
.. 这对这三辆车来说，可真是个大挑战啊。
'.. a pretty tall order for
three cars like these.'

922
00:52:40,720 --> 00:52:43,920
这感觉像坐在Zulu上一样，看它们向我们冲来。
It's like Zulu, watching
them coming towards us.

923
00:52:50,800 --> 00:52:52,270
来啦。
Here we go.

924
00:52:53,960 --> 00:52:57,000
有人有计划吗？我可没啊。
Has anyone got any
plans, cos I haven't?

925
00:52:58,320 --> 00:53:01,950
'Hammond建议我们把牛群分成小块。
'Hammond suggested we break
the herd into smaller chunks.

926
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:04,750
'但根本没起作用。
'But that didn't work at all.'

927
00:53:04,800 --> 00:53:07,880
它们现在完全跑错方向了。
They're going in completely
the wrong direction now.

928
00:53:12,360 --> 00:53:15,660
哦，现在……它们怎么了……？什么？它们已经……
Oh, now... How are they...?
What, they've gone...

929
00:53:22,120 --> 00:53:25,550
它们就在我周围转，根本不怕我。
They're just going round me.
They are not very scared of me.

930
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:29,870
我被牛群围在中间，搞砸了。
I'm in the middle. I've been herded
by the cows. It's all gone wrong.

931
00:53:29,920 --> 00:53:34,390
~ 克拉克森，你到底在哪儿？  
~ 我现在在牛粪里。
~ Clarkson, where the hell are you?
~ I am now in cow dust.

932
00:53:34,440 --> 00:53:36,240
我啥也看不见。
I can see nothing.

933
00:53:37,440 --> 00:53:39,790
好啊，它们向我冲来，真是意外。
OK, they're charging
me. This is unexpected.

934
00:53:39,840 --> 00:53:42,040
它们冲向我。
They're running towards me.

935
00:53:43,440 --> 00:53:47,400
我们被牛群围住了，输给了牛。
We are in the middle of the cows.
We've been outwitted by cows.

936
00:53:49,640 --> 00:53:52,670
呃，好牛啊。早安，牛儿们。
Um, nice cows. Morning, cows.

937
00:53:52,720 --> 00:53:54,790
那头公牛在威胁我。
That bull's menacing me.

938
00:53:59,040 --> 00:54:01,270
这牛真是胆子大得惊人。
This is a remarkably brave cow.

939
00:54:01,320 --> 00:54:03,910
它根本不回队列。
It won't be pushed
back into line at all.

940
00:54:03,960 --> 00:54:06,700
我说的“牛”，指的可是巨大的公牛。
When I say "cow",
I mean massive bull.

941
00:54:09,360 --> 00:54:13,470
我这里可能需要点帮助，这家伙真是倔得一匹。
I may need some help here.
This guy is properly stubborn.

942
00:54:13,520 --> 00:54:15,750
我就叫你James May吧。
I shall call you James May.

943
00:54:15,800 --> 00:54:17,940
他更怕尼桑。
He fears the Nissan more.

944
00:54:18,880 --> 00:54:23,270
'结果发现，那并不完全准确。'
'And as it turned out, that
wasn't entirely accurate.'

945
00:54:25,080 --> 00:54:27,020
他冲我撞上来了！
He's head-butting me!

946
00:54:30,840 --> 00:54:33,040
他猛撞了你的达特桑。
He head-butted your Datsun.

947
00:54:36,360 --> 00:54:38,990
'与此同时，回到宾利那边……'
'Meanwhile, back in the Bentley...'

948
00:54:40,760 --> 00:54:42,320
Jeremy！
Jeremy!

949
00:54:43,800 --> 00:54:46,390
'显然，情况并不妙，
'Clearly, things weren't going well,

950
00:54:46,440 --> 00:54:48,510
'于是我们做了个决定。
'so we made a decision.'

951
00:54:50,760 --> 00:54:53,470
我觉得这群牛太多了。
I think there are too many for us.

952
00:54:53,520 --> 00:54:55,190
嗯，是啊。
Well, yes.

953
00:54:55,240 --> 00:54:57,470
我们需要骑兵支援。
We need the cavalry.

954
00:54:57,520 --> 00:55:00,640
'十分钟后，支援终于来了。'
'And ten minutes later, it arrived.'

955
00:55:08,840 --> 00:55:10,750
哈哈哈！
Ho-ho-ho!

956
00:55:10,800 --> 00:55:13,430
世界上最危险的职业之一，
One of the most dangerous
jobs in the world,

957
00:55:13,480 --> 00:55:16,720
驾驶罗宾逊直升机赶牛。
flying the Robinson helicopters
to muster the cattle.

958
00:55:17,960 --> 00:55:21,190
平均每年大约会宰掉八头。
On average, round about eight
are killed every year.

959
00:55:21,240 --> 00:55:25,920
有时他们会用滑橇把牛逼进队列。
Sometimes they will use the skids
to actually push the cows into line.

960
00:55:28,560 --> 00:55:33,600
'有了空中吊舱支援，我们终于把局面收拾起来。'
'With the air cav as backup, we
started to get our act together.'

961
00:55:36,200 --> 00:55:39,430
哈蒙德，你负责应付崎岖地形的反应。
Hammond, you're the rough
terrain response.

962
00:55:39,480 --> 00:55:41,550
而我负责快速反应。
And I'm the quick response.

963
00:55:41,600 --> 00:55:43,830
不错，还行。
That's good, that's good.

964
00:55:43,880 --> 00:55:46,750
让它们冲进去，我来把车往前开。
Channel 'em in, I'll
drive them forwards.

965
00:55:50,680 --> 00:55:53,190
侧翼，侧翼。
Flanking, flanking.

966
00:55:53,240 --> 00:55:54,830
上吧，往左走。
Go on, go left.

967
00:55:54,880 --> 00:55:57,150
♪ 我在骑马…… ♪
♪ I was riding my horse... ♪

968
00:55:59,160 --> 00:56:00,760
在右边刹车。
Braking right.

969
00:56:01,760 --> 00:56:04,100
干得好，哈蒙德，干得好。
Good work, Hammond, good work.

970
00:56:05,600 --> 00:56:10,150
那辆宾利横穿田野，真是壮观。
That Bentley going across that
field is a sight to behold.

971
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:12,540
看看……看看它的轮子！
Look at... Look at its wheels!

972
00:56:14,840 --> 00:56:17,190
‘很快，我们意识到点什么。’
'Soon, we realised something.'

973
00:56:17,240 --> 00:56:19,640
啊，来啦，看那儿。
Ah, there you go. Look at that.

974
00:56:21,720 --> 00:56:26,110
‘难得《顶级机车》这次有野心，没那么烂。’
'For once, Top Gear was being
ambitious and not rubbish.'

975
00:57:56,520 --> 00:58:00,030
~ 好啊，牛仔！ ~ 我感觉很男人！
~ All right, cowboy!
~ I feel pretty manly!

976
00:58:00,080 --> 00:58:02,480
我感觉像那头公牛一样。
I feel like one of those bulls.

977
00:58:07,560 --> 00:58:09,990
~ 我超喜欢的。 ~ 我觉得很爽。
~ I loved that.
~ I thought that was fun.

978
00:58:10,040 --> 00:58:13,510
~ 真是太好玩了。 ~ 是啊。 ~ 还有这些车……
~ That was a lot of fun.
~ It was.
~ And these cars...

979
00:58:13,560 --> 00:58:16,430
~ 比马强多了。 ~ 而且没人掉下来。 ~ 好多了。 ~ 嗯。
~ better than horses.
~ And nobody fell off.
~ Much better.
~ Yeah.

980
00:58:16,480 --> 00:58:17,870
不过我们能先停一下吗？
But can we just stop for a moment?

981
00:58:17,920 --> 00:58:21,670
惊人的是——车子竟然挺住了。啥也没坏，三台全完好。
The amazing thing - the cars survived
it. Nothing broke. All three.

982
00:58:21,720 --> 00:58:24,750
太棒了。要是日产……哦不，其实是宾利或宝马，
Fantastic. And if Nissan... well,
actually, or Bentley or BMW,

983
00:58:24,800 --> 00:58:28,150
要是他们造笔记本，我马上买。
if they made a laptop, I'd buy it.

984
00:58:28,200 --> 00:58:31,590
你可以把日产笔记本扔厕所，登录一下……
You could throw a Nissan laptop
in the lavatory, do a log on it...

985
00:58:32,880 --> 00:58:35,110
……还能继续登录。
.. and you'd still be
able to log on on it.

986
00:58:35,160 --> 00:58:36,950
你说得对。总之……
You would. Anyway...

987
00:58:37,000 --> 00:58:41,110
现在该决定这几台车谁最牛了。
we must now decide which
of these cars is the best.

988
00:58:41,160 --> 00:58:43,470
好啊，我不退让。是宾利。
Well, I'm not backing
down. It's the Bentley.

989
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:46,390
我不退让。就是这台日产。
I'm not backing down.
It is this Nissan.

990
00:58:46,440 --> 00:58:49,590
詹姆斯，抱歉，兄弟，你彻底错了。
James, sorry, mate.
You are just wrong.

991
00:58:49,640 --> 00:58:52,710
这台日产GT‑R，带点纽博格林的味道。
The Nissan GT-R, it has a
whiff of the Nurburgring.

992
00:58:52,760 --> 00:58:56,030
不是一点点味儿，是全身散发！
It's not just a whiff of the
Nurburgring. It reeks of it!

993
00:58:56,080 --> 00:58:58,990
坐进去后，你的衣服六周后还能闻到味儿。
Your clothes will smell of it six
weeks after you've been in it.

994
00:58:59,040 --> 00:59:01,710
总比闻到瑞恩·吉格斯的浴水味好。
It's better than it smelling
of Ryan Giggs's bath water.

995
00:59:01,760 --> 00:59:04,510
兄弟，那是宾利啊。
Mate, it's a Bentley.

996
00:59:04,560 --> 00:59:07,430
~ 想想这意味着什么。 ~ 我告诉你这意味着啥，哈蒙德。
~ Think what that means.
~ I'll tell you what it means, Hammond.

997
00:59:07,480 --> 00:59:12,630
这就是说它比这贵了六万六千英镑。
It means it is £66,000
more expensive than this.

998
00:59:12,680 --> 00:59:15,910
是啊，因为那是日产！那是宾利。
Yes, because that's a Nissan!
That's a Bentley.

999
00:59:15,960 --> 00:59:18,910
没错。那是日产。而把这台日产全部拆光后，
Exactly. It's a Nissan. And when you
strip everything off this Nissan,

1000
00:59:18,960 --> 00:59:20,670
下面竟然是一辆赛车。
you find underneath a racing car.

1001
00:59:20,720 --> 00:59:23,150
把那辆宾利的所有装饰全剥掉，
When you strip all the
stuff off of that Bentley,

1002
00:59:23,200 --> 00:59:25,870
底下其实就是一辆大众。
underneath it is a VW.

1003
00:59:25,920 --> 00:59:28,510
如果把你的全部装饰都剥掉，
If we strip all the stuff off you,

1004
00:59:28,560 --> 00:59:30,870
我们会发现底下是一副同样的基本骨架
we'd find underneath
the same basic skeleton

1005
00:59:30,920 --> 00:59:32,910
就跟赛车手的骨架一样。
as you would find in a racing driver.

1006
00:59:32,960 --> 00:59:35,710
不过把所有东西重新装回去后，必须把你装成詹姆斯·梅，
But when we put it all back on,
as we must, to make you James May,

1007
00:59:35,760 --> 00:59:37,950
你就是詹姆斯·梅！这根本不是那辆车。
you're James May! That's
the wrong car.

1008
00:59:38,000 --> 00:59:40,550
好啊，哈蒙德，但要是把你全剥光，
Yes, but, Hammond, if we stripped
everything off of you,

1009
00:59:40,600 --> 00:59:44,350
我们会发现你和赛车手小时候的骨架一模一样！
we'd find the same skeleton that you have
in a racing driver when he was a little boy!

1010
00:59:44,400 --> 00:59:47,550
不过把它们重新拼起来，你仍然是理查德·哈蒙德。
But when you put it all back together,
you are still Richard Hammond.

1011
00:59:47,600 --> 00:59:52,390
你穿那辆GT‑R，就跟你穿那双鞋子一样。
You in that GT-R is like
you in those shoes.

1012
00:59:52,440 --> 00:59:53,550
荒唐！
Ridiculous!

1013
00:59:53,600 --> 00:59:58,710
这话可是那位身披 100% 纯正 1935 织物夹克的家伙说的。
Says the man in the jacket
woven out of 100% pure 1935.

1014
01:00:00,560 --> 01:00:03,790
它的设计目的非常明确——
That was designed very
specifically for a purpose -

1015
01:00:03,840 --> 01:00:06,070
就是在性能的极限边缘让人爽到不行。
to feel good on the ragged
edge of performance.

1016
01:00:06,120 --> 01:00:07,990
你可没法做到。
You're not going to do that.

1017
01:00:08,040 --> 01:00:09,910
你手上有块能上月球的手表。
You have a watch that
can go to the moon.

1018
01:00:09,960 --> 01:00:11,470
但你永远也上不了月球。
You're never going to go to the moon.

1019
01:00:11,520 --> 01:00:14,430
他们根本不生产你尺寸的月球靴，但你就是喜欢那块手表
They don't make moon boots in your
size, but you like having that watch

1020
01:00:14,480 --> 01:00:16,670
因为这说明它是一块好手表。
because it means it is a good watch.

1021
01:00:16,720 --> 01:00:18,590
车子也是同理。
And it's the same with the car.

1022
01:00:18,640 --> 01:00:20,840
~ 你只是在装个 ~ 哔——。
~ You're just being a
~ BLEEP.

1023
01:00:24,240 --> 01:00:25,710
谢谢。
Thank you.

1024
01:00:26,760 --> 01:00:29,670
~ 你还有个
~ 哔——
~ 像个
~ 哔—— 哔——。
~ And you've got a
~ BLEEP
~ like a
~ BLEEP BLEEP.

1025
01:00:29,720 --> 01:00:32,390
一个小号的。
A baby one.

1026
01:00:32,440 --> 01:00:33,950
各位先生，先生们，先生们，
Gentlemen. Gentlemen, gentlemen,

1027
01:00:34,000 --> 01:00:36,430
抱歉，我得在这里打断一下，
I'm sorry, I'm going to have
to interrupt at this point,

1028
01:00:36,480 --> 01:00:37,870
因为事实是，
because the fact of the matter is,

1029
01:00:37,920 --> 01:00:42,670
不管你用什么可量化的方式衡量，宝马都是最佳座驾。
by any measurable means you choose,
the BMW is the best car.

1030
01:00:42,720 --> 01:00:45,230
~ 可是… Y…
~ 我才不会买呢。
~ But... Y...
~ But I wouldn't buy one.

1031
01:00:45,280 --> 01:00:46,310
好啊，为什么？
Well, why?

1032
01:00:46,360 --> 01:00:50,350
因为快速又贵的宝马，一买下来价值立刻暴跌。
Because fast, expensive BMWs plummet
in value as soon as you buy them.

1033
01:00:50,400 --> 01:00:51,670
你买了其中一辆，
You buy one of those,

1034
01:00:51,720 --> 01:00:54,830
不到十八个月就会亏掉四万、五万英镑。
within 18 months you are going
to lose £40,000, £45,000.

